d hunts. Perhaps they'll require the players deal with cruel forest gods that demand unreasonable sacrifices? Protip: Don't piss off the people producing the food for your population.<br /> - the nationalists in Exalted could be what amounts to the exalt's &quot;fanclub&quot; in the kingdom: They think the exalts rock, but only as long as they make the country better than the neighbouring countries. Failing that, they'll be pissed and might want the old regime back.<br /> - the religious faction in Exalted doesn't need much explanation. Perhaps the kingdom the exalts conqured/liberated/whatnot has a lot of people who worship the immaculate dragons. How are they going to make peace with those people? Diplomacy? Appeasement? mind control? Is one temple demanding favorable treatment over another?<br /> - the communists, in Exalted, would be representatives for the workers in the cities. They don't own any land, and perhaps they were worked to the bone by the old king to produce weapons or goods for export. They want better working and living conditions, more pay, all that jazz... and perhaps the wealth of the country depends on their industrial output, so... better not piss them off, right? but perhaps their demands will eat too much into your profits?<br /> - the aristocracy. You might have taken over from the evil king, but what about the nobles of the land? Do they trust you as the new ruler? Will they switch aligeance to neighboring kings or warlords if you come off as too weak? who knows<br /> - the merchants. as rulers, how will you deal with the guild? You need them to buy goods your country produces, but they want special tax exemptions, and you like taxing things now. remember: the guild always plays dirty, but do you dare anger them by calling them on their bullshit? Only a foolish warlord makes an enemy of the guild, for suddenly your enemies will be able to buy weapons, horses and mercenaries at great discounts, while drug dealers will start appearing all over your territories.<br /> - if the players just delegate power to a governor who rules in their place... remember: a ruler who is never there, perhaps always off on adventure, might not recognize what he or she comes back to one day. Perhaps you're not even in charge when you return home one day.<br /> <br /> Each of these are a potential plot hook for some kind of adventure. Perhaps there are other secret organizations operating in the kingdom that later reveal themselves, now that its the players who are in charge?<br /> <br /> oh well<br /> <br /> TL<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />R - if you are unsure of how to deal with players who have gained great power.... then go see how they wield that power, and make the game about that for a bit. Will they become tyrants? Will they become selfless champions of the people? Cult leaders?</div> </div> </div> </div>What if the entire population is brainwashed and any dissenters get death rayed? What then ? What do you do when the PCs are the real monsters not the \u201cantagonists\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12796,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","user":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","date":". 07-17-2019, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T01:17:28-07:00","id":1325515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324266-essence-3-celestials-what-do-you-do-when-you-have-too-much-power?p=1325410#post1325410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the entire population is brainwashed and any dissenters get death rayed? What then ? What do you do when the PCs are the real monsters not the \u201cantagonists\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I pick it up and run with it. I like the idea of Solars becoming monsters.<br /> <br /> For some groups it might be time to retire the characters and have the old PCs become the new BBEGs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T09:51:08-07:00","id":1325630,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the concept of having the method and the consequences being more the focus than the means of victory, but I don\u2019t think the two are mutually exclusive. In fact I think one can even help facilitate the other. For example if you\u2019re summoning Octavian and the Princes, that could label you unfavourably as women and men who consort with the fel powers powers of Malfeas. That\u2019s only really a choice to be made if the task at hand is so difficult or dangerous that not summoning them would risk failure. I think it could also add weight to otherwise interesting choices. Like let\u2019s say your circle battles long and hard through the freezing tundra of a northern winter, trying to recover a stone that will purify any water it\u2019s submerged in, so that you can bring it home, clean your defiled lake and save your people from having to migrate elsewhere. Unfortunately, when you get there you discover a hidden little civilization nestled around an otherwise toxic volcanic geyser, using the stone to purify it for their crops and drinking. Now that\u2019s already an interesting choice, but it\u2019s even weightier if the PC have suffered for months to get here, and likely will for months on the journey back either way, and what\u2019s all that for? For nothing? And not even because the legends were wrong, their salvation is right there, they\u2019d just be condemning these people to death by taking it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also there can be a bit of an issue with Solars being so powerful that the consequences of their actions also are easily taken care of. For example if you\u2019re labeled demon summoners and your zenith just says \u201cwait guys, we\u2019re actually still cool\u201d and backs that up with solar magic, then that problem just goes away. Not to mention with have multiple big complex systems for social interaction, combat, crafting ect. Which kind of implies that we\u2019re supposed to be using them in interesting ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 07-18-2019, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T10:14:04-07:00","id":1325640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324266-essence-3-celestials-what-do-you-do-when-you-have-too-much-power?p=1325515#post1325515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pick it up and run with it. I like the idea of Solars becoming monsters.<br /> <br /> For some groups it might be time to retire the characters and have the old PCs become the new BBEGs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d be curious to hear more on your take as to how you would run with it .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:13:22-07:00","id":1325661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324266-essence-3-celestials-what-do-you-do-when-you-have-too-much-power?p=1325630#post1325630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate the concept of having the method and the consequences being more the focus than the means of victory, but I don\u2019t think the two are mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree, and never meant to suggest otherwise! There are absolutely times when a serious challenge is appropriate, and can add drama. My point was more that the questions of consequences and uses of power should generally be the larger source of dramatic tension, not the <i>only</i> source. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also there can be a bit of an issue with Solars being so powerful that the consequences of their actions also are easily taken care of. For example if you\u2019re labeled demon summoners and your zenith just says \u201cwait guys, we\u2019re actually still cool\u201d and backs that up with solar magic, then that problem just goes away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but I feel 3e has actually largely addressed this issue by cutting out a lot of the &quot;you just win&quot; or &quot;affect giant swathes of Creation&quot; charms that 2e had. Now, you generally do have to get in there and engage with individual NPCs to solve a lot of your problems. For example, if the circle has gained a rep as demon summoners, even someone with Supernal Presence or Socialize can't just wave their hands and say &quot;Actually, everyone feels we're still good&quot;. They would have to get out and actually talk to all those people, or, at very least, send competent minions to do so. And that has consequences of its own - every minute spent convincing the common people that you're one of the <i>nice</i> demon summoners is time not spent talking to the envoy from the neighboring queendom who wants a trade deal oh and by the way, what's all this about demon worship? And successfully convincing the people that you're nice demon summoners has knock-on effects too - it makes it easier for someone else to come in and claim that <i>they're</i> nice demon summoners too, or even that demon worship in general isn't such a bad thing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention with have multiple big complex systems for social interaction, combat, crafting ect. Which kind of implies that we\u2019re supposed to be using them in interesting ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, and I'm not advocating for dispensing with those systems. What I'm suggesting, however, is that expecting most interactions with such systems to result in success, often extreme success, on the part of the players should be the default, and that trying to source all your drama and tension on the assumption that they <i>won't</i> succeed is going to be disappointing, because Exalted isn't really built that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T14:41:33-07:00","id":1325737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324266-essence-3-celestials-what-do-you-do-when-you-have-too-much-power?p=1325515#post1325515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pick it up and run with it. I like the idea of Solars becoming monsters.<br /> <br /> For some groups it might be time to retire the characters and have the old PCs become the new BBEGs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is the correct answer<br /> <br /> will the guild dare send merchant caravans to their lands - knowing that the population are mind-slaves, and that their merchants might suffer the same fate? That can ruin your economy as foreign trade dries up<br /> <br /> that kind of mass brain-washing is sure to attract a ton of attention from neighboring warlords who might start to get really worried. And of course it'll provoke a MASSIVE wyld hunt! Perhaps a whole realm legion! As useless as the realm regent is, then he knows damn well that nothing unites the realm as well as a good ol' common enemy - and sending a legion or two towards a kingdom overtaken by anathema?<br /> <br /> ...which will also mean that there'll be sidereals involved, probably both gold and bronze faction. What does the gold faction think of the player's actions? Do they still think they're redeemable? Or are they just going to 'feed' the circle to the bronze faction and let them send dream-assassins or something similarly impossible to defend against.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is part of what I love about Exalted: It doesn't matter how powerful you get - there will always be something more powerful that can be dug up from the lore.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Mahasuchi hears of the players and finds them a threat - how well can the players defend a highly intelligent lunar warlord using guerrilla warfare against them? A solar with kickass powers is still only able to be in one place at a time... five attacks coordinated to take place at the same time - can't save everything. What will the players prioritize to protect? The farming community? (if not, enjoy the food shortages in three months) The plantation producing stuff they need for industry? (if not, enjoy the material shortfalls soon) The mine? (I hope you don't need iron for your weapons industry) The capital city outskirts (just how terrified do you want your population?)<br /> <br /> just make sure that there are options and ways for your players to actually come out on top - this should NEVER be structured purely as punishment to the players. This is exalted after all, rule of cool and whatnot - but you don't have to tell your players that. If they've gotten so paradigm locked into thinking that only them as a team of adventurers can solve things, without delegating... then show them that they can't be everywhere at once - teach them to delegate - or conversely if they rely too much on delegation, then remind them that sometimes you need to handle things personally.<br /> <br /> <br /> And if the players are heavily into mind-controling their population - then consider how robust or weak the mind control is. How exactly is the mind control done? What'll happen if a clever guild merchant shows up somewhere in their nation and convincingly claims to represent the players, demanding all kinds of goods and money turned over to him. Will the players realise that a population without free will is an open invitation for exploitation? Or perhaps the mind control makes the population highly xenophobic? Or maybe the mind control has conflicting orders baked into it - making people's minds lock up on occation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hell, if the players become tyrants... maybe they'll attract another circle of solars who want to save the kingdom from the evil tyrants - and thus the story can come full circle, especially the players end up going &quot;wait... are we the baddies?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T16:41:58-07:00","id":1325769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324266-essence-3-celestials-what-do-you-do-when-you-have-too-much-power?p=1325515#post1325515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pick it up and run with it. I like the idea of Solars becoming monsters.<br /> <br /> For some groups it might be time to retire the characters and have the old PCs become the new BBEGs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternative answer; Let the players continue to prove The Immaculate Order correct in calling them anathema.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T00:57:16-07:00","id":1325903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inertial Frame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324266-essence-3-celestials-what-do-you-do-when-you-have-too-much-power?p=1325769#post1325769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternative answer; Let the players continue to prove The Immaculate Order correct in calling them anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me the great inspirations for Solars are (Dustin Hoffman's titular role) Hook, Saitama (One Punch Man), Light Yagami (Deathnote), Ozymandias (Watchmen) and Emperor Palpatine (Star Wars).<br /> <br /> If you're not hitting notes of tragically overcompetent hero tinged with remorselessly efficient monster then you're not playing the same Exalted I am.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Order is correct. From a certain point of view.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> &quot;I think a bit of skulduggery would do you good. Take your mind off this ennui business. First thing tomorrow morning, we'll shoot some Dynasts out at Harbourhead.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm tired of killing Dynasts and Fae. I always kill them. I've been killing them my whole life!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-19-2019, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T11:57:54-07:00","id":1326055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324266-essence-3-celestials-what-do-you-do-when-you-have-too-much-power?p=1325737#post1325737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that kind of mass brain-washing is sure to attract a ton of attention from neighboring warlords who might start to get really worried. And of course it'll provoke a MASSIVE wyld hunt! Perhaps a whole realm legion!</div> </div> </div> </div>3 realm legions.<br /> <br /> Though I think they'd have come anyway. The mind control is fairly subtle, everything else about that sorceress is not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if the players are heavily into mind-controling their population - then consider how robust or weak the mind control is. How exactly is the mind control done? What'll happen if a clever guild merchant shows up somewhere in their nation and convincingly claims to represent the players, demanding all kinds of goods and money turned over to him. Will the players realise that a population without free will is an open invitation for exploitation? </div> </div> </div>I did consider impersonating the sorceress, but there wasn't really much point. She was the one we were worried about, not her underlings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell, if the players become tyrants... maybe they'll attract another circle of solars who want to save the kingdom from the evil tyrants </div> </div> </div>Too many social characters it would seem. They invited a lot of Solars to a big conclave. Some they got to join them, others are just grumbling and shouting.<br /> <br /> I should explain that some of the PCs actually do consider the mind-control sorceress a tyrant and would like to get rid of her. Though for now it looks like they're just going to let the Realm do it for them (which will mean the Realm controls a set of mountains right above the other PCs' lands...).<br /> Of course, they are also tyrants, so it's entirely hypocritical, but in different ways. I'd argue the sorceress is probably only the second-worst.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - and thus the story can come full circle, especially the players end up going &quot;wait... are we the baddies?&quot; </div> </div> </div>Oh, half the players already know that. I mean, one guy describes his character as &quot;Djala Hitler&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T22:04:14-07:00","id":1326612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324266-essence-3-celestials-what-do-you-do-when-you-have-too-much-power?p=1325661#post1325661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps, but I feel 3e has actually largely addressed this issue by cutting out a lot of the &quot;you just win&quot; or &quot;affect giant swathes of Creation&quot; charms that 2e had. Now, you generally do have to get in there and engage with individual NPCs to solve a lot of your problems. For example, if the circle has gained a rep as demon summoners, even someone with Supernal Presence or Socialize can't just wave their hands and say &quot;Actually, everyone feels we're still good&quot;. They would have to get out and actually talk to all those people, or, at very least, send competent minions to do so. And that has consequences of its own - every minute spent convincing the common people that you're one of the <i>nice</i> demon summoners is time not spent talking to the envoy from the neighboring queendom who wants a trade deal oh and by the way, what's all this about demon worship? And successfully convincing the people that you're nice demon summoners has knock-on effects too - it makes it easier for someone else to come in and claim that <i>they're</i> nice demon summoners too, or even that demon worship in general isn't such a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, and thank god 3e does that much better than 2e, <i>but </i>you have to admit that it's when the players are running up against things that they can't instantly fix that that the interesting things happen. The difference is just what those things are.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324266-essence-3-celestials-what-do-you-do-when-you-have-too-much-power?p=1325661#post1325661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, and I'm not advocating for dispensing with those systems. What I'm suggesting, however, is that expecting most interactions with such systems to result in success, often extreme success, on the part of the players should be the default, and that trying to source all your drama and tension on the assumption that they <i>won't</i> succeed is going to be disappointing, because Exalted isn't really built that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we might be talking about different things. Generally, I like seeing my players succeed, I expect them to succeed and even in systems like DnD or Call of Cthulhu I can happily complete entire campaigns without my PCs failing once at anything they try to do. Barring maybe inconsequential failures like missing out on a little coin purse with 25gp in it hidden under a bench or what have you.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that the puzzles or social scenes or battles were challenging though. They faced truly worthy foes in their stories.<br /> <br /> Where that didn't happen was the third game of 3e that my group ran, where one of the players was a Solar sail supernal who had, I think around 20 sail charms, maybe more, by the end of the game. With all those charms he increased the speed, doubled maneuverability, rerolled 1s, doubled 9s, treated his opponent's 1s as his own 10s, free autosuccesses, negated all penalties, all sorts of crazy stuff and it was just so, so pointless. There's no antagonist in the book, or any book until DBs got released, that could even come close, and even with DBs I'm not sure how close it would be.<br /> <br /> It's fun at first, but it's fun in the way of turning on god mode in a video game is fun and just having a chuckle as you walk around having bullets bounce off of you like Superman. It wasn't very long before even he got bored of it though. Instead of the climactic battle of the Flying Duchman against the Black Pearl swirling around the enormous maelstrom, playing a game of one-upping the other by dipping deeper down into it for more speed, bellowing orders to his crew, guffawing like a madman in the face of certain death as the ships trade fierce blows, what he got was the music starting up, the sky darkening, the two ships bearing down on eachother, and then he blows right through the other in one ram like it was cardboard and the fight's over.<br /> <br /> It is a cold comfort to that player, who never once got to have their fun sea captain adventure of navigating deadly reefs or battling wicked pirates played out, to tell them that the battle was a forgone conclusion anyway and it just fast tracked us to the real game which is dealing with the consequences of it. It just makes so much of the game so meaningless, that you wonder why we bother with it at all when we could just go play the Godsend shard of the Legacy RPG or something, which is totally diceless and just runs off a kind of &quot;You pick a thing, it happens, but maybe other things also happen&quot; setup.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Also apologies if I seem frustrated with you, I'm not, just with mostly former problems with Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 07-22-2019, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T16:33:55-07:00","id":1327814,"title":"","content":"To echo what some othere people have been saying.<br /> The illusion of threat is more important than the immediate danger everything posesses. As the Storyteller you control all offscreen variables and you need to find the sweetspot where you're trusted enough to not murder all their friends and loved ones in a temper tantrum but also able to exploit the disparity in knowledge when you know what the PCs can do but they don't know what your NPCs are capable of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T08:20:02-07:00","id":1327902,"title":"","content":"Wait what pcs have friends ? Your better of threatening stuff they really care about like things they own. If your pcs are notorious assholes they not going to have any friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T08:48:46-07:00","id":1327908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324266-essence-3-celestials-what-do-you-do-when-you-have-too-much-power?p=1327902#post1327902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait what pcs have friends ? .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All PCs in any game I have STed for the last six years or so in any system I have STed? Damn it, in my current Urban Fantasy-Horror campaign, &quot;My NPC sister is transgender and I don\u00b4t know how to help her&quot; and &quot;I have a broken heart due to loving the wrong NPC person&quot; are actual, important plot points. Any game worth its salt care for these things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13031,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","user":"Clophiroth","date":". 07-28-2019, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}